        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

<p class="text-text-mid text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">THDi (total harmonic distortion of current) quantifies how far a current waveform has strayed from a pure sinusoid because of harmonics. It is the single number that decides whether a low-voltage (LV) bus meets IEEE 519 &mdash; and whether your transformers and cables are quietly overheating. This article explains what THDi is, where it comes from, what it costs, and how an active harmonic filter (AHF) cancels it.</p>
<h2 id="what-thdi-is" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">What THDi Is</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">Harmonics are current and voltage components at integer multiples of the fundamental (50 or 60 Hz). THDi is the RMS sum of those harmonics divided by the RMS fundamental, expressed as a percentage:</p>
<blockquote class="border-l-4 border-brand-orange pl-4 italic text-text-mid my-6">THDi = &radic;(&#931; I_h&sup2;) / I_1 &times; 100%</blockquote>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">Below about <strong>5%</strong> the waveform is close to ideal; above about <strong>20%</strong> it is severely distorted. IEEE 519 caps LV <strong>THDi &lt; 5%</strong> (individual harmonics &lt; ~3%) at the point of common coupling (PCC).</p>
<h2 id="how-thdi-happens" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">How THDi Happens</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">The cause is nonlinear loads &mdash; devices that draw current in abrupt pulses rather than smoothly. Common sources include:</p>
<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mb-6 text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
  <li>Variable-frequency drives (VFDs)</li>
  <li>LED lighting</li>
  <li>Computers and office equipment</li>
  <li>UPS systems</li>
  <li>Switch-mode power supplies</li>
  <li>Battery chargers and EV chargers</li>
</ul>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">A six-pulse rectifier &mdash; the front end of most VFDs and UPS units &mdash; generates characteristic harmonics at orders <strong>n = 6k &plusmn; 1</strong>: the 5th, 7th, 11th, and 13th. Left untreated, THDi at the load often sits between <strong>8% and 30%</strong>.</p>
<h2 id="what-high-thdi-costs" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">What High THDi Costs</h2>
<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mb-6 text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
  <li><strong>Overheating</strong> &mdash; harmonic current raises I&sup2;R loss in cables and transformers with the square of current, so they age faster.</li>
  <li><strong>Reduced power factor</strong> &mdash; distorted current lowers true PF, raising apparent power and the bill.</li>
  <li><strong>Equipment malfunction</strong> &mdash; PLCs, sensors, and communications error out on a distorted bus.</li>
  <li><strong>Protective-device interference</strong> &mdash; breakers and fuses misoperate on a distorted waveform.</li>
  <li><strong>Resonance</strong> &mdash; harmonic current can resonate with system capacitance and inductance, amplifying voltage.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="how-to-reduce-thdi" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">How to Reduce THDi</h2>
<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mb-6 text-text-mid leading-relaxed">
  <li><strong>Passive filters</strong> &mdash; tuned to block specific orders; economical for fixed spectra but resonance-prone.</li>
  <li><strong>AHF</strong> &mdash; dynamically injects counter-current to cancel distortion in real time.</li>
  <li><strong>K-rated transformers and line reactors</strong> &mdash; help hardware survive harmonics.</li>
  <li><strong>Load balancing</strong> &mdash; cuts neutral current and the associated triplen harmonics.</li>
  <li><strong>Low-THD equipment</strong> &mdash; complying with IEEE 519 and IEC 61000-3-2 at the source.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="the-ahf-fix" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">The AHF Fix</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">An AHF samples the load current, separates the fundamental from the distortion, and injects the inverse:</p>
<blockquote class="border-l-4 border-brand-orange pl-4 italic text-text-mid my-6">i_c* = i_L &minus; i_s(fundamental)</blockquote>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">Synthesized by a bridge switching at 15&ndash;20 kHz, it tracks within <strong>&lt; 1 ms</strong> and pulls THDi from <strong>30%+ down to &lt; 5%</strong> across the 5th through 25th orders simultaneously. It also compensates reactive current and helps balance phases, with no resonance risk.</p>
<h2 id="igbt-vs-sic" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">IGBT vs SiC</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">Most LV AHFs use IGBTs with a junction capped near <strong>150 &deg;C</strong>. Silicon-carbide (SiC) MOSFETs widen the bandgap (<strong>3.26 eV vs 1.12 eV</strong>), tolerate <strong>200 &deg;C</strong>, switch at <strong>2&ndash;3&times;</strong> the frequency, and cut switching loss by roughly <strong>50%</strong> &mdash; a smaller, cooler cabinet with headroom for higher orders. That is the direction CHITEK's LV AHF platform is built on.</p>
<h2 id="engineering-deployment-checklist" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">Engineering Deployment Checklist</h2>
<ol class="list-decimal text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6 pl-5 space-y-2">
  <li>Measure at the PCC over a full duty cycle with a power-quality analyzer.</li>
  <li>Place the AHF at the source &mdash; on the feeder feeding the nonlinear cluster.</li>
  <li>Audit capacitor banks for resonance before commissioning.</li>
  <li>Size on measured TDD referenced to peak demand.</li>
  <li>Leave headroom (15&ndash;25%) for added load.</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="bottom-line" class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-barlow-condensed)] text-text-dark mt-10 mb-4">Bottom Line</h2>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">THDi is the number that tells you whether your bus is clean or quietly degrading. A low-voltage <strong>AHF</strong> cancels the distortion at the source &mdash; measurably, within IEEE 519. CHITEK’s LV AHF platforms are specified from exactly this measurement-first discipline.</p>
<p class="text-text-mid leading-relaxed mb-6">What THDi is your bus actually logging &mdash; and is it under 5% at the PCC?</p>

